ce and  isn't something to be sneezed at  many capital cities are asking  themselves what's going to happen to all  the vacant commercial real estate  the final industry related factor is  covert induced burnouts which have  mostly affected the fields of technology  and healthcare both have seen  significant increases in resignations  throughout the pandemic and for good  reason  it's no secret that healthcare workers  were under unprecedented amounts of  pressure every day  workloads have been increased through  hospital overcrowding and due to the  nature of the virus staff shortages due  to sick leave for skyrocketing and for  many nurses doctors and support staff  this pressure simply was too much to  cope with this led to a 4.5 increase in  healthcare resignations over the past  year  on top of all of this there were also  those who weren't happy with the vaccine  mandates and chose to resign as a  consequence  there are also factors outside of  industry that play a role such as age  and career progression  according to the us bureau of labor  statistics resignation rates are the  highest among mid-career employees those  between the ages of 30 and 45  generally staff turnover rates are the  highest among 20 to 25 year olds but due  to a greater level of financial  insecurity among younger age  demographics resignations have slightly  decreased in that group in recent years  it's also been suggested that for a  number of those in the 30-45 age  demographic  covert was just the final push towards  resignation that employees had been  considering for some time  the prudential pulse of american worker  survey conducted in may of 2021 found  that 53 percent of workers would retrain  for a different industry or career if  they had the opportunity  before we continue let's take a look at  our morning brew update it appears that  the stock markets have had enough of  covert the so-called stay-at-home growth  stocks are now suffering netflix  shoplift and others are all affected but  the biggest loss is by peloton an  exercise bike company in may of 2021  they wanted to build a 400 million  factory to meet all the demand of  at-home work equipment since then 2 800  jobs have been cut and the stock has  plunged 82  needless to say those plans are now  toast if you want more stories like this  one be sure to check out morning brew  it's a daily newsletter that gets you  all the latest news in the one place  delivered straight to your inbox each  day of the week  it's free and takes just 15 seconds to  sign up so click the link below to get  started  with waves of resignation letters  flooding to the desks of employers  widespread labor shortages were  inevitable to this day it's rare to see  a business in the service industry  without help wanted signage on their  window  at first the conversation turned to  blaming welfare and laziness with  employees assuming that staff would  eventually come to their senses and all  of this would just blow over  it didn't  an anecdotal example of the way  attitudes have shifted is the rise of  followers and activity in the reddit  forum anti-work the forum is a place for  people to share their experiences of  poor working conditions expose  exploitative companies and discuss  alternative systems to the standard nine  to five in october of 2020 the page had  a modest 180 000 followers today that  number has risen to nearly 1.8 million  some news outlets such as the new york  post have even gone as far as to say  that the anti-work subreddit is partly  to blame for the great resignation  over in the u.s there have been some  strange consequences for schools due to  staff shortages the national guard has  been deployed to some schools personnel  have been given orders to drive school  buses and teach classrooms definitely an  odd site  with the labour shortage being felt  across the globe employees are getting  desperate with some offering strange  incentives to entice new staff  companies have straight up begun to  offer cash for applicants to make it to  the interview stage like one frankfurt  based tech company whose name i can't  pronounce who is offering 500 euros for  anyone who makes it to interviews  another 1 000 euros for those who make  it to the second round and 5 000 to  those who complete six months probation  in the us target and other brands have  announced that they would pay college  tuition and textbooks for new workers  who also want to pursue studies  in a win for fast food workers  mcdonald's announced in 2021 that it was  going to increase wages by 10 to combat  labor shortages but this was specified  only to mcdonald's own stores and not  the franchise restaurants which make up  the majority  when that didn't work some mcdonald's  stores in the us were offering new  employees a free iphone if they stayed  with the company for more than six  months  the hand of other employees have been  forced to increase benefit packages  offer more flexible working schedules  boost mental health programs and in some  cases the permanent increase in wages  these efforts all point to a clear shift  in power but only time will tell how  long the shift would last  some are seeing the great resignation  evolving into something slightly  different moving forward  australian treasurer joss freidenberg  believes that the great resignation will  more likely resemble a great reshuffle  and will ultimately be a positive for  the economy as people switching jobs  allows for upward class mobility  while quit rates are still quite high  some economists are predicting that a  course correction is incoming in an  interview at fortune.com behavioural  economist and professor at the wharton  school of the university of pennsylvania  iwan narenke said that covert  restrictions easing should lead to a  return to normalcy  as for low wage industries it's harder  to know how the great resignation will  affect employee employer relationships  minimum wage increases are a constant  topic of discussion and while that was  amplified by the pandemic any lasting  changes are yet to be seen particularly  in the u.s market  while inflation is also rising there is  also a risk of a wage price spiral  upwards but for now we'll just have to  wait and see  as the world adopts to a post-covert  life and billionaires continue to build  rockets for fun  public awareness of class divides will  only grow deeper because of this i think  it's safe to predict that how many  companies hire and retain staff and how  employees seek out and accept work may  just have changed for good  so this will be an interesting one to  throw to you guys  in the comments section share your  experiences with employment and work  over the past two years  tell us about what's happening in your  industry and what changes that you've  noticed  through all the comments and discussion  we might be able to get a clearer  understanding of how this is affecting  people globally though as always if you  do want to discuss this in more detail  head over to the cold fusion discord  before i go just a quick announcement  it's a long story but i basically had to  start up a new cold fusion facebook page  so if you're still on facebook check it  out the link will be in the description  i'll be posting some exclusive podcast  clips from a new podcast i'm starting up  with one of my friends i'll play you one  of those clips now to see you out  alright cheers guys have a good one also  ai companions so um if you've ever seen  the movie her yes it's got the earpiece  so um that's becoming a reality  essentially there's um an ai companion  called replica and it's kind of um  taking off uh  for younger people because people are  feeling lonely at the moment and um so  basically learned your conversation  likes and wants and talks to you and  asks you about your day and  um yeah also in southeast asia there's a  few others that are taking off and i  think it's just it's inevitable when you  just went to some black mirror [ __ ] it  is there was a black mirror episode  exactly on this where she recreated her  dead boyfriend  um  but yeah i think it's inevitable when  the ai's got to a point where it's just  good enough but you know in two years  time because in um  japan they already have um anime  girlfriends you can create  difference from anime cartoons right um  yeah you can like easily marry them as  well in some places don't know about  that well it's probably true but  yeah actually yeah  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  cold fusion  it's new thinking


